      "body": "## Overview\n\nCombine the two `return_sampling_mask` request-admission checks into one actionable `ValueError`, document the contract on the flag, and warn at config verification. Fixes #61318.\n\n## Claims\n\n- A request that fails both `temperature > 0` and `top_k > 0` gets a single error listing both unmet conditions (with current values).\n- A request that only fails `top_k` still gets a clear single-condition message (no false temperature complaint).\n- Valid params (`temperature > 0`, `top_k > 0`) still pass admission.\n- `ModelConfig.return_sampling_mask` docstring states both requirements.\n- Enabling the flag logs a startup warning that every request must use `temperature > 0` and `top_k > 0`.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  tests/test_sampling_params.py::test_return_sampling_mask_reports_all_unmet_preconditions \\\n  tests/test_sampling_params.py::test_return_sampling_mask_reports_top_k_alone \\\n  tests/test_sampling_params.py::test_return_sampling_mask_accepts_valid_params \\\n  tests/test_config.py::test_sampling_replay_config \\\n  tests/test_config.py::test_sampling_replay_config_warns_about_request_preconditions \\\n  -v\n# 20 passed\n```\n\nReproduced the split-raise path on `main` via `InputProcessor._validate_params` (no GPU): `temperature=0` then `temperature=0.7` without `top_k` failed one check at a time. After this change, the first case lists both conditions in one message.\n\n## Details\n\n**Root cause:** `_validate_params` raised separate `ValueError`s for temperature and `top_k`, so clients discovered the full contract by trial and error. The flag is engine-level, but nothing at config time said every request needs those params.\n\n**Approach:** Collect unmet conditions and raise once. Expand the field docstring (feeds CLI help). Warn in `_verify_sampling_replay_config` so operators see the contract before the first rejected client call. No change to which requests are accepted or rejected.\n\n**Not duplicating:** No open PR references #61318.\n\nAI assistance was used to draft the change, tests, and this PR description. The human submitter reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above.\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
